LED FILAMENT ROD  --  old-tech mapping + electrical fundamentals

TYPE
  Modern name : LED filament (chip-on-glass / chip-on-sapphire)
  Old analog  : selenium rectifier STACK  (many junctions in series)
  Not         : cat whisker, 1N34 single diode, tungsten filament, resistor

PHYSICAL
  core        : thin glass/sapphire strip ("white strip")
  devices     : ~24-31 blue InGaN LED dies in SERIES
  coating     : YAG:Ce (and sometimes red) phosphor in silicone  (the yellow)
  look off    : yellow rod, pale strip inside
  look on     : warm-white glowing bar (~2700 K typical)

ELECTRICAL TYPE
  device class      : semiconductor PN junctions, series string
  conduction        : one-way (diode), strongly non-ohmic
  unbiased LCR      : high R, small C (tens-hundreds pF), tiny L (~10-50 nH)
  forward operating : Vf_string ~ 70-85 V DC @ I_f ~ 10-12 mA
  power             : P ~= Vf * If  ~ 0.8-1.2 W per rod
  polarity          : marked by construction; reverse = dark + stress

VARIABLES (one rod, typical decorative bulb)
  N          number of dies in series          ~ 25 to 30
  Vf_chip    forward voltage per blue die      ~ 2.8 to 3.2 V
  Vf         string forward voltage            Vf ~= N * Vf_chip  ~ 80 V
  If         recommended forward current       ~ 10 to 12 mA
  P          operating power                   P = Vf * If
  rd         dynamic resistance dV/dI on       ~ a few hundred ohms near 10 mA
  Rs         metal-trace series resistance     a few ohms
  C_dark     unbiased string capacitance       C_die / N
  L          geometric series inductance       tens of nH
  Rth        thermal resistance (in bulb)      ~ 60 C/W class (helium-cooled)

FUNDAMENTALS
  Ohm's law does NOT hold as a constant R.
  Below Vf the string is nearly open.
  Above Vf current rises steeply; MUST current-limit.
  Equivalent at one operating point only:
      R_eq = Vf / If    (example: 80 V / 0.010 A = 8 kOhm)   <-- not a real resistor
  Small-signal (ON):
      Z(w) ~= Rs + rd / (1 + j*w*rd*C) + j*w*L
  Phosphor is electrically insulating; current is only in the dies + traces.
  AC raw across the string = half-wave conduction + reverse stress + flicker.
  Drive with DC (or pulsed DC), correct polarity, limited current.

FOUR RODS FROM ONE BULB
  parallel     : ~80 V,  40-50 mA total
  two pairs    : ~160 V, 20-25 mA total
  all series   : ~320 V, 10-12 mA total

OLD-TECH CHEAT SHEET
  cat whisker          point-contact detector      NO
  1N34 / crystal diode single low-Vf junction      only 1/Nth of this
  selenium rectifier   series junction STACK       YES, closest
  neon lamp            high strike voltage glow    similar voltage-feel only
  Edison tungsten      hot ohmic wire              appearance only

WILL NOT LIGHT FROM
  crystal radio / antenna  (uW to mW, << 1 W and << 80 V)

CAN LIGHT FROM
  solar + battery/storage + boost + current limit
  target: ~80 V DC @ ~10 mA per rod
